# Snyk (https://snyk.io) policy file, patches or ignores known vulnerabilities.
version: v1.5.0
ignore:
  SNYK-JAVA-COMFASTERXMLJACKSONCORE-20059179:
    - '*':
        reason: >-
          No released version fixes this: introduced by flyway-core's
          jackson-dataformat-toml dependency on jackson-core@2.17.2.
          Same as the other jackson findings here - no published Maven
          Central release actually fixes it (verified 2026-09-27); real
          fix requires bumping flyway-core to a newer major version,
          tracked as a separate upgrade task.
        expires: 2026-12-15T00:00:00.000Z
  SNYK-JAVA-COMFASTERXMLJACKSONCORE-20059683:
    - '*':
        reason: >-
          No released version fixes this: Snyk lists 2.18.11/2.21.7/2.22.3
          as fixed versions, but none exist on Maven Central as of
          2026-09-27 (latest real jackson-databind release is 2.19.0,
          which remains vulnerable). Introduced via jjwt-jackson's
          jackson-databind dependency. Revisit once Jackson ships a real
          fix.
        expires: 2026-12-15T00:00:00.000Z
  SNYK-JAVA-COMFASTERXMLJACKSONCORE-15365924:
    - '*':
        reason: >-
          No released version fixes this: com.fasterxml.jackson.core is
          already pinned via Spring Boot's jackson-bom (2.17.2), and none of
          the versions Snyk lists as fixing it (e.g. 2.18.8, 2.18.10, 2.21.4)
          have actually been published to Maven Central as of 2026-09-15 -
          the latest real jackson-databind/jackson-core release is 2.19.0,
          which remains vulnerable. Revisit once Jackson ships a real fix.
        expires: 2026-12-15T00:00:00.000Z
